    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25637" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laetābundus</span></b> , a, um,
			adj.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>greatly rejoicing, full of joy, joyful</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">laetabundus is dicitur, qui abunde laetus est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell. 11, 15, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">his dictis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Mart. Cap. 1, § 23</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. Isa. 35, 2</span></i>.</div>
